   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of children (under 15) on ART among all children living with HIV at the end of the reporting period</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">It should be noted that the HIV estimates change every year and the denominators will change each subsequent year based on latest estimates then; and those current figures will be used as
denominators. The baseline for this indicator is 70.2% (59,172/84,295) (HMIS, 2019). Targets: The targets used to inform the PFR are derived from the 2019 Estimates. Targets are based on
expected number of children on treatment as at the end of 2020, and the net monthly enrolment. Treatment for children is funded 100% with resources from the the Global Fund and Pepfar (3600).
Note: Targets in the ZNSP IV were based on 2018 estimates and vary from the PF targets which used the 2019 Estimates. In addition, the quantification used the 2018 Estimates. The 2018
Estimates has higher targets than 2019 Estimates, hence we have quantified for more children than required. The figures will be realigned with 2019 HIV estimates. Source for Reporting:
(numerator): ART Register and DHIS2 (The report is submitted monthly). EPMS and/or eHR to the ART Registers are additional sources Source for Reporting (denominator): HIV estimates
EPP/Spectrum</narrative>
    </description>
