   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of adults (15 and above) on ART among all adults living with HIV at the end of the reporting period</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The indicator measures adults who are currently on ART at the end of each reporting period. In line with the 2020 WHO/GF SI Guidelines, this indicator measures progress towards providing ART to
all PLHIV, i.e. treatment coverage, taking in to account total attrition during the reporting period. Numerator: Number of adults (15 and above) on ART at the end of the reporting period Denominator:
Estimated number of adults (15 and above) living with HIV (From HIV estimates) Targets: These are national targets: 92% (2021), 93% (2022) and 94% (2024) from ZNASP 2021-2025 (available
resources currently cover 1,143,681 for each of the 3 years). Provision has been made in the PAAR to support the gap and this has been approved by TRP as a priority when efficiencies are
realized (FYI - in NFM2 GF approved savings were used to fund gaps in treatment). Baseline: The baseline has been derived from pogramme data (numerator) and 2019 HIV estimates
(Denominator). Source for Reporting (numerator): ART Register and DHIS2. The report is submitted monthly. EPMS and/or eHR to the ART Registers are additional sources. Source for reporting
denominator: HIV estimates Note: When reporting, the consolidated results will be presented, in addition to disaggregated results by age and sex (male and female) in line with the WHO/GF SI
Guidelines: &#x2022; Age; &#x2022; Gender (female, male); &#x2022; Gender | Age - (female 15+, male 15+, female 15-19, male 15-19, female 20-24, male 20-24, female 15-24, male 15-24) &#x2022; Newly initiating ART</narrative>
    </description>
