   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV O-11??? Percentage of people living with HIV who know their HIV status at the end of the reporting period</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program acknowledges that the most effective way to ensure that people living with HIV are aware of their HIV status is to continue offering HIV testing services
(HTS) at locations and among populations with the highest HIV burden. HTS is the entry point to the continuum of care as it measures the progress towards increasing
proportion of people living with HIV who know their HIV status. Numerator: Number of people living with HIV who have been diagnosed with HIV and received their
results. Denominator: Estimated number of people living with HIV The indicator baseline and targets were informed by the National HIV Estimates (2019/20). The targets
have been aligned with the revised ZNASP IV Results Framework 2021-2025. Targets for 2021-2023 are 92%, 93%, 94% resp. Results will be estimated based on HIV
case program data which includes case-based surveillance data (as the numerator) and the national PLHIV estimates based on annual spectrum modelled results.
During reporting, the results will be dissagregated by the recommended data categorization by Age and Gender. Source of reporting: MoHCC Program Data and the Annual HIV Estimates- Spectrum Modelling</narrative>
    </description>
